config BR2_PACKAGE_FPLINUX_TYRQUAKE
	bool "fplinux-tyrquake"
	depends on BR2_USE_MMU
	help
	  Build TyrQuake 0.71 with native FPLinux fbdev and
	  evdev backends. The software renderer derives its mode
	  from the RGB565 framebuffer geometry, rotates portrait
	  displays into landscape and scales only when the panel is
	  smaller than TyrQuake's minimum render size. The explicit
	  input mode selects the phone or host source; evdev identity
	  and capabilities only validate that source. Sound, CD audio
	  and networking are disabled.

	  The launcher uses a fixed 32 MiB heap and one input
	  mode: the phone keypad or the forwarded host keyboard.
	  Game data is not included. A user-supplied pak0.pak is
	  read from /mnt/card at run time.
